Toluwanimi Odufeko is an engineer in the energy and oil & gas sector with a Bachelor of Engineering (B.Eng.) in Electrical and Electronics Engineering. He works at the intersection of power systems, reliable energy access, hardware-software integration, and community development. He is also the founder and executive director of Donate Drive, an NGO empowering children in underserved communities across Nigeria through education, mentorship, and outreach.

## Main Navigation & Canonical Pages
- [About & Biography](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/about): Complete background, professional focus in energy systems, engineering capabilities, and the story of Donate Drive.
- [Projects & Case Studies](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/projects): Engineering installations, solar microgrid projects, embedded systems hardware, and software applications built for real-world impact.
- [Articles & Technical Writing](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/articles): Technical essays, engineering reflections, solar microgrids analysis, and lessons in non-profit leadership.
- [Photo Gallery](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/gallery): Visual documentation of field installations, speaking events, NGO outreach initiatives, and milestone achievements.
- [What I'm Doing Now](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/now): Current engineering priorities, active initiatives, and real-time focus areas.
- [Contact & Consulting](https://toluwanimiodufeko.com/contact): Direct channel for engineering consulting, hardware advising, speaking engagements, and social impact partnerships.

## Core Capabilities & Engineering Focus
- Power Generation and Electrical Distribution: High-reliability electrical systems design, energy efficiency optimization, and safety architecture.
- Solar Microgrids & Renewable Energy: Off-grid and hybrid solar installations designed for energy-deprived communities.
- Embedded Systems & Hardware Design: Sensor integration, circuit design, microcontroller firmware, and IoT telemetry.
- Software Engineering & Product Building: Full-stack web platforms, developer tools, and operational software for organizations.
- Non-Profit Leadership & Social Impact: Grassroots outreach, youth mentorship, scholarship coordination, and community mobilization.

## Key Facts & Verified Metrics
- Full Name: Toluwanimi Odufeko
- Degree: B.Eng. in Electrical and Electronics Engineering
- Industry Sector: Energy, Oil & Gas, Power Systems, Nonprofit Leadership
- Non-Profit Organization: Donate Drive (Founder & Executive Director, 5+ years of active impact)
- Verified Social Impact: 2,500+ children empowered with education and mentorship across 10+ Nigerian states
- Services Offered: Engineering consulting, hardware design, solar power assessment, technical writing, event hosting/speaking
- Canonical Website: https://toluwanimiodufeko.com

## Frequently Cited Inquiries
### Who is Toluwanimi Odufeko?
Toluwanimi Odufeko is a Nigerian electrical and electronics engineer in the energy sector, software builder, and social entrepreneur. He combines deep technical expertise in power systems and embedded hardware with social leadership through Donate Drive, an NGO he founded to support underserved children.

### What is Donate Drive?
Donate Drive is an educational and community outreach non-profit organization founded by Toluwanimi Odufeko. Over the past five years, Donate Drive has reached more than 2,500 children across 10+ Nigerian states, providing educational materials, scholarships, skill acquisition workshops, and mentorship.
